  "justification": "The proposed architecture scales the EC2 tier from t3.micro (40 req/s per instance) to t3.small (80 req/s per instance) and increases the ASG maximum from 4 to 10 to meet peak load of 750 req/s at origin. With 2 instances at baseline (150 req/s average: 2 × 80 = 160 req/s capacity) and up to 10 instances at peak (750 req/s: 10 × 80 = 800 req/s capacity with headroom), the web tier scales automatically. The RDS instance type upgrades from db.t3.micro to db.t3.medium to sustain increased application database load. Multi-AZ replication on both instances provides automatic failover meeting RTO and RPO requirements via 7-day backup retention and point-in-time recovery. NAT Gateway, ALB, CloudFront, and S3 remain unchanged. The architecture meets all six requirements: N1 peak 750 req/s and baseline 150 req/s are sustained via Auto Scaling; N2 high availability is ensured by Multi-AZ RDS failover and dual-AZ EC2 deployment; N3 RPO/RTO are met through automated backups and Multi-AZ failover; N4 CloudFront demand is costed at 2,000 GB and 40 million requests; N6 Auto Scaling web tier is retained. Total cost is $748.38/month, within the $750 budget.",
