  "justification": "The original architecture cannot sustain peak load of 750 req/s at origin (1,500 req/s ÷ 2 CloudFront cache hit rate). Two t3.micro instances provide only 80 req/s, 87 percent short of requirement. Upgrading to t3.small instances (80 req/s each) provides 160 req/s baseline (sufficient for 150 req/s average) and scales to 800 req/s at ASG max of 10 instances, meeting the 750 req/s peak. The proposed BOM shows steady-state cost for 2 t3.small instances always-on plus Auto Scaling capacity up to 10 instances to handle peak demand during the 60 peak hours per month. Database remains db.t3.micro Multi-AZ to satisfy N2 (automatic failover across AZs), N3 (PITR with 7-day retention for RPO ≤5 min, RTO ≤1 hour via automatic failover), and cost constraints. CloudFront configuration updated to match N4 (2,000 GB, 40M requests). Total proposed cost $305.94 is within $750 budget. Auto Scaling elasticity ensures high availability and on-demand capacity for peak demand while minimizing idle cost.",
