  "stated_original_monthly_cost_usd": 328.35,
  "stated_proposed_monthly_cost_usd": 715.66,
  "justification": "The original architecture cannot sustain the peak load of 750 requests per second at the origin tier. With t3.micro instances at 40 req/s per instance at 70% CPU, the maximum 4 instances deliver only 160 req/s, falling 590 req/s short of the 750 req/s requirement (N1). Upgrading to t3.small instances (80 req/s each) allows the ASG to reach 10 instances maximum, providing 800 req/s capacity—exceeding the 750 req/s peak demand while maintaining the required minimum of 2 instances across 2 AZs for high availability (N2).\n\nThe database configuration retains db.t3.micro with Multi-AZ failover, which is sufficient because the peak database load is driven by application logic, not transaction throughput. Multi-AZ replication provides automatic failover meeting the 1-hour RTO requirement (typically 1–2 minutes). Point-in-time recovery (PITR) with 5-day retention enables database recovery to any point within 5 minutes, meeting the 5-minute RPO (N3). CloudFront demand increases from 200 GB to 2,000 GB and from 5 million to 40 million requests (N4), driving higher CloudFront costs. The proposed architecture costs $715.66/month, remaining within the $750 budget (N5) with $34.34 of contingency. The design maintains an EC2 Auto Scaling web tier as required (N6).\n\n**Well-Architected Framework:**\n\n*Operational Excellence:* PITR with 5-day retention and Multi-AZ automatic failover eliminate manual recovery work; automated ASG scaling adjusts capacity based on demand without operator intervention; CloudWatch integration provides visibility into peak load periods and scaling events.\n\n*Security:* Multi-AZ configuration maintains AZ isolation; private subnets with NAT gateway control outbound traffic; RDS Multi-AZ encrypts cross-AZ replication; no relaxation of existing security controls.\n\n*Reliability:* Multi-AZ database failover completes in < 2 minutes, satisfying RTO; continuous automated backups with 5-day PITR satisfy RPO; minimum 2 instances across 2 AZs ensure web tier survives single-AZ failure; ASG self-healing replaces failed instances automatically.\n\n*Performance Efficiency:* t3.small instances deliver 2× throughput of t3.micro at 2× hourly cost; ASG scales to only 2 instances during average-load periods (150 req/s origin demand requires 2 instances at 80 req/s each), reducing waste relative to running maximum capacity; CloudFront caches 50% of requests, cutting origin load from 1,500 to 750 req/s at peak.\n\n*Cost Optimization:* ASG minimum of 2 instances during off-peak (670 hours) and flexible scaling during peak (60 hours) distributes compute cost; t3.small provides sufficient capacity at manageable cost; monthly total of $715.66 is 4.6% below budget, leaving room for growth.",
  "comparison": "**Original Architecture (Stage 3):**\n- Stated cost: $328.35/month\n- Compute: t3.micro (40 req/s per instance), ASG min 2 / max 4 = 160 req/s maximum origin capacity\n- Peak load gap: 750 req/s required − 160 req/s available = 590 req/s shortfall; architecture fails to meet N1\n- Database: db.t3.micro Multi-AZ; no explicit PITR or backup retention policy stated\n- Reliability: HA at web tier and database; automatic failover; recovery objectives not explicitly configured\n- CloudFront: 200 GB, 5M requests per month\n\n**Proposed Architecture:**\n- Stated cost: $715.66/month (within $750 budget)\n- Compute: t3.small (80 req/s per instance), ASG min 2 / max 10 = 800 req/s maximum origin capacity\n- Peak load capacity: 800 req/s available − 750 req/s required = 50 req/s headroom; meets N1 with margin\n- Database: db.t3.micro Multi-AZ with 5-day PITR and backup retention; meets N3 (5-min RPO, 1-hour RTO)\n- Reliability: HA maintained; automatic failover; explicit recovery policies configured\n- CloudFront: 2,000 GB, 40M requests per month (matches N4 demand)\n\n**Cost Impact:**\n- Monthly increase: $715.66 − $328.35 = +$387.31 (117.9% increase)\n- Primary drivers: t3.small instances cost 2× t3.micro; CloudFront costs scale 10× (GB and requests both increase 10×)\n- Off-peak cost mitigation: ASG scales down to 2 t3.small instances (2 × 80 = 160 req/s), equivalent capacity to 4 t3.micro instances, during low-demand periods\n- Budget compliance: $750.00 − $715.66 = $34.34 remaining"
}
